id: try_divide
category: exceptions
difficulty: 4
libs:
checker: exact
timeout: 10
--- prompt
Write an Objeck program that divides the integer 10 by a variable holding 0 inside a try block and catches the division error with an `on` clause for the DivideByZeroError type, printing `caught` in that clause. A finally block must print `done`. Output must be `caught` then `done` on separate lines.
--- expected
caught
done
--- reference
class TryDivide {
	function : Main(args : String[]) ~ Nil {
		zero := 0;
		try {
			result := 10 / zero;
			result->PrintLine();
		}
		on(e : DivideByZeroError) {
			"caught"->PrintLine();
		}
		finally {
			"done"->PrintLine();
		};
	}
}
